            <ArticleTitle>Vocal tremor: where are we at?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>475-479</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/MOO.0000000000000412</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="PURPOSE OF REVIEW" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">Vocal tremor in movement disorders is often overlooked, although it has a significant impact on quality of life. Careful observation of tremor phenomenology allows for accurate diagnosis and tailored treatment.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RECENT FINDINGS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">The central pathways associated with various vocal tremor-associated diseases have been further elucidated.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="SUMMARY" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Patients are likely to benefit from a combination of medical and interventional treatments delivered within a multidisciplinary setting.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
